{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You are El of seeing.</b> Pointed with a ḥataf qamatz, because it is a noun — 'the El of seeing,' who sees in the humiliation of the humiliated.'" "<b>Have I even here.</b> An expression of astonishment: 'Was I so presumptuous as to think that even here in the wildernesss I would see the emissary of the Omnipresent — after seeing them in the house of Abraham, where I was accustomed to seeing angels?' And know that she was accustomed to seeing them, for Manoah saw the angel once and said, מוֹת נָמוּת (Judges 13) — but she saw four, one after another, and was not terrified."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:57.167630055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}